---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { formatDate } from '../lib/posts';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';

const updated = new Date(`${SITE.nowUpdated}T00:00:00Z`);
---

<Base
  title="Now"
  description="What Deion Menor is working on, reading, and learning right now."
  current="now"
>
  <header class="page-header">
    <p class="eyebrow">Now</p>
    <h1>What I'm doing now</h1>
    <p class="page-intro">
      A snapshot of my focus at the moment, not a biography. Last updated{' '}
      {formatDate(updated)}.
    </p>
  </header>

  <div class="prose now-page">
    <h2>Building</h2>
    <p>
      A small set of web tools, this site among them. I'm rewriting a side
      project so that the whole thing fits in my head at once: fewer services,
      fewer dependencies, and a database I can hold in a single file.
    </p>

    <h2>Writing</h2>
    <p>
      Working through a longer essay about defaults — why the settings we never
      touch shape our work more than the ones we obsess over. Shorter notes go
      up here as they're ready.
    </p>

    <h2>Reading</h2>
    <p>
      <em>The Art of Doing Science and Engineering</em> by Richard Hamming, one
      chapter at a time. I keep returning to his point that the important thing
      is not the answer but the habit of asking better questions.
    </p>

    <h2>Learning</h2>
    <p>
      How far one Postgres database can go before it needs company. So far: much
      further than I assumed, and with fewer moving parts than the alternatives.
    </p>

    <h2>Not doing</h2>
    <p>
      Adding more tools to my workflow. Fewer tabs, smaller systems, and a
      shorter list of things I'm pretending to maintain.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
